# Plan: DropUI React port (`drop-ui-react`)

## Context

DropUI is an Angular 22 drag & drop UI builder. The existing persistence plans in `drop-ui/.claude/plans/` already say the app will be ported to other frameworks as separate projects sharing one backend. This plan covers the React port.

Decisions made with the user:

- **Location:** a new sibling repo, `C:\Users\telis\Repos\drop-ui-react`. The Angular repo is not modified.
- **State:** Zustand.

Goal: feature parity with the Angular app as it is in the working tree today (palette, grid layout panel, multi-cell canvas, drag/reorder/move, edit text, delete), proven by the same three test suites. The three Playwright files in `drop-ui/e2e/` are the acceptance contract: they are copied over and must pass without changes to their assertions.

Size of the port: 6 components + root, 1 store, 3 model files, 14 test files, 3 e2e files.

## Stack

Versions are the current `latest` on npm (checked 2026-10-04).

| Angular today | React port | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Angular 22, `@angular/build` | **React 19.3** + **Vite 8** + `@vitejs/plugin-react` 6 | TypeScript ~6.0 as now |
| `@ngrx/signals` SignalStore | **Zustand 5** | see Store below |
| `@angular/cdk/drag-drop` | **`@dnd-kit/core` 6 + `@dnd-kit/sortable`** | pointer-event based, so the e2e `drag()` helper works unchanged |
| `@angular/cdk/menu`, `@angular/cdk/dialog`, overlay, focus trap | **Base UI** (`@base-ui/react` 1.x) `Menu` and `Dialog` | unstyled, styled with the same DaisyUI classes |
| Signal Forms (`form`, `validate`) | plain `useState` + derived `invalid` | one field; no form library |
| `inject()` DI | React context + hooks | only the store needs it |
| RxJS (dialog results) | none | dialogs become controlled components |
| `@angular/router` (empty routes) | none | add a router when a route exists |
| Tailwind 4 + DaisyUI 5 | same, via `@tailwindcss/vite` | `styles.css` carries over minus the CDK imports |
| Vitest 4 via `@angular/build:unit-test` | Vitest 4 directly, two `projects` | jsdom + browser (`@vitest/browser-playwright`) |
| `@testing-library/angular` | `@testing-library/react` 16 + `@testing-library/jest-dom` | same `render` / `screen` API |
| Playwright | Playwright | same config, different port |

Optional: enable the React Compiler (`babel-plugin-react-compiler` 1.0) in `vite.config.ts` for automatic memoization. Not required for parity.

`@angular/aria` is in `package.json` but not imported anywhere in `src/`, so it needs no equivalent.

